  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \n\nSurface high pressure remains centered just south of the Ohio Valley \nand anomalous upper level ridging stays anchored in place through at \nleast Thursday. Hot and humid conditions persist. Forecast highs in \nthe lower to middle 90s, along with dew points in the middle 70s, \nresult in peak heat index values around the 105 mark with higher \nreadings possible. An Extreme Heat Warning is in place through \nThursday to account for the high heat and humidity. Overnight lows \nin the 70s offer little relief from the heat.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \n\nRidging may start to break down on Friday allowing chances for \nconvection and less confidence in the extreme heat. However, \nconditions will still be hot and humid through the holiday weekend. \nOutdoor activities could see some impacts from isolated to scattered \nthunderstorm activity especially during the afternoon and evening \nhours.",
